# Architecture — segments

What goes into each segment across slice layers (modules, widgets, pages). See [`architecture/layers.mdc`](./layers.mdc) for where slices live.

Etalons in code: `src/4_modules/Auth` (segmented module) and `src/3_widgets/Header` (flat widget). Copy those shapes; do not invent `ui/` or `api/`.

Intra-slice import flow:

```
presentation → model → data
                 ↘     ↙
                  domain
```

`domain` imports nothing. `presentation` does not import `data` — the network reaches the UI through `model` (interactor).

### `presentation`

React UI and its view-model.

- Lives here: `*.component.tsx`, colocated `*.component.m.css`, `*.vm.ts` next to the component they drive.
- May import: `shared`, `core`, the slice's `model`. Not `data`, not `domain`.
- Must not contain: interactors, HTTP, domain types, or business rules.

### `model`

Application use-cases of the slice.

- Lives here: interactors (`*.interactor.ts`) that orchestrate `data`, and form/app schemas (`*.schema.ts`).
- May import: `shared`, `core`, the slice's `data` and `domain`. Not `presentation`.
- Must not contain: React, view-models (those live in `presentation`), or raw HTTP (that lives in `data`).

### `data`

Network boundary of the slice.

- Lives here: API classes (`*.api.ts`) — `mobx-tanstack-query` `Mutation`/`Query`, `HttpClient`, abort signals.
- May import: `shared`, `core` (query client), the slice's `domain`. Not `presentation`, not `model`.
- Must not contain: UI, interactors, or domain rules.

### `domain`

Pure domain — types and rules with no infrastructure.

- Lives here: interfaces (`*.interface.ts`) and pure predicates. Etalon: `IPhone`.
- Must not import anything — no `shared`, no `core`, no other segments, no side-effecting libs (enforced by `no-restricted-imports`).
- Must not contain: API calls, stores, view-models, or React.

### `lib` / `config` / `constants`

Optional. Slice-local helpers, config objects (`C*` + `*.config.ts`), and scalar constants. Create only when the slice needs them. Do not put view-models, interactors, or API classes here.

## Flat widgets (no segment folders)

A widget that is one component + view-model stays flat at the slice root — etalon `Header`: `Header.component.tsx`, `Header.vm.ts`, `Header.component.m.css`, `index.ts`. Add `presentation/`/`model/` only when the widget outgrows that.
